      </div>
      <div class="rollout-step">
        <div class="rollout-num">2</div>
        <h3 class="rollout-title">Configure</h3>
        <p class="rollout-desc">POS, integrations, and fiscal rules configured per market: NF525, TSE, VAT, and GST built in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rollout-step">
        <div class="rollout-num">3</div>
        <h3 class="rollout-title">Train</h3>
        <p class="rollout-desc">Associates are serving customers in under 30 minutes, no classroom sessions, no thick manuals.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rollout-step">
        <div class="rollout-num">4</div>
        <h3 class="rollout-title">Go live</h3>
        <p class="rollout-desc">White-glove launch support, onsite or remote: single store, global fleet, or pop-up, at your pace.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rollout-step">
        <div class="rollout-num">5</div>
        <h3 class="rollout-title">Stay supported</h3>
        <p class="rollout-desc">A dedicated team that knows your business and picks up when you call: real humans, not a ticket queue.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rollout-foot">
      <i class="ti ti-circle-check-filled"></i> Support is never outsourced to a call center. You work directly with the people who built the platform, alongside whichever partners you bring to the program.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ BLOG ============ -->
<section class="ac-magenta section" style="padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 72px;" aria-label="Latest insights">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Blog</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Retail commerce insights and news.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Perspectives on point of sale, unified commerce, RFID, and mobile retail, from the team behind the platform.</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Driven from the blog collection, not hardcoded. Three posts were hardcoded here
         with hand-written excerpts, and they drifted: all three pointed at posts that did
         not exist on teamworkcommerce.com, and two repeated research claims that could not
         be sourced. Reading from the collection means these cards can only ever show real
         published posts, with the post's own words. -->
    <div class="blog-grid">
      {% for post in collections.blogpost | recentPosts(3) %}
      <a href="{{ post.url }}" class="blog-card{% if loop.first %} featured{% endif %}" style="text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="blog-card-img">
          <img src="/assets/images/blog/real/{{ post.fileSlug }}.jpg" alt="{{ post.data.title }}" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="blog-card-body">
          <div class="blog-card-meta">
            <span class="blog-tag{% if loop.first %} featured{% endif %}">{% if loop.first %}Featured{% else %}{{ post.data.category or "Blog" }}{% endif %}</span>
            <span class="blog-card-date">{{ post.data.date | formatDate }}</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="blog-card-title">{{ post.data.title }}</h3>
          <p class="blog-card-excerpt">{{ post.data.dek or post.data.description }}</p>
          <span class="pillar-link">Read article <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></span>
        </div>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">
      <a href="/blog/" class="btn btn-ghost">View all posts <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

